        "v": 5,
        "title": "Fix stagePatches to skip deleted files",
        "summary": "stagePatches in common/src/util/git.ts now filters file paths using fs.existsSync before executing git add. This prevents errors when attempting to stage files that have been deleted from the working directory. The function returns false if no existing files remain to stage. Unused imports for os and diff were removed.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:43:04.858Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The software that prepares your changed files for saving now skips over any files you've already deleted from your computer, so it won't trip over missing files and leave the rest unstaged. If every file in a batch was deleted, the staging step reports that nothing was prepared rather than erroring out. This is already live and affects anyone using the assistant to apply edits.",
