      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant can now reach the o1 model through a single external routing service instead of talking to OpenAI directly, which means responses still come from o1 but travel over a different connection. OpenRouter now handles o1 requests, so the team added a new key it checks for at startup and updated the planning step that prepares answers. You would only notice this if you were already using the o1 preview feature, because the switch happened quietly behind the scenes and the assistant still produces the same kind of answer.",
